    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "I’ve always found math interesting but not deeply connected to my daily life. As a vocational student, I use basic math in practical contexts like budgeting or measurements. I enjoy its logic, especially in economics and history, where patterns and data matter. I don’t see it as a subject I need to master, but rather one that helps me understand the world better.",
    "Do you ever get anxious when thinking about mathematics?": "Not really. I’ve never felt overwhelmed by math, even in complex topics. My low neuroticism and calm mindset help me stay relaxed. I focus on understanding concepts rather than memorizing formulas. If something feels hard, I take a break or try a different approach—like using board games to think through problems. Anxiety doesn’t come up often, and I prefer to stay curious and patient.",
    "Did you ever use AI to support your math learning in the last year? If yes, how was your experience?": "Yes, I used a simple AI tool last year to check my economics calculations. It helped me verify my work and explain steps clearly. I didn’t use it for advanced math, but it boosted my confidence in basic problem-solving. The experience was positive—simple, fast, and helpful. I’d recommend it for students who want quick feedback without stress.",
